   "insight": {
    "headline": "A broad decline, not a rotation",
    "body": "Only 9 of 44 large caps closed higher, which makes this a broad fall rather than money moving between sectors. Materials took the worst of it — Grasim, Tata Steel and UltraTech all off more than 3% — while telecom (+2.5%) and pharma (+0.9%) held up. Both are classic defensives: people keep paying phone bills and buying medicine when the cycle turns. The rupee slipped again to 95.42. When breadth is this narrow, the index number understates the damage, because a handful of large names mask how many stocks actually fell."
