   "insight": {
    "headline": "Risk appetite returned, but only in tech",
    "body": "21 of 35 mega caps rose, the Nasdaq gained 1.73% and the VIX fell 6.1% to 14.5. The VIX measures how much investors are paying for downside protection, so a fall means fear easing. Note the split: the Dow was flat at −0.08% while the Nasdaq ran, which tells you the buying was concentrated in technology rather than broad-based. Energy led the sectors at +3.5% while industrials lagged at −1.6%. Today's biggest movers are earnings reactions — Workday +17.8%, Cellebrite −29.2% — which is what an active results season looks like."
