   "insight": {
    "headline": "Textbook defensive rotation",
    "body": "The Hang Seng fell 2.15% with technology down 5.5% on average — Tencent −8.1%, Meituan −5.4%, Xiaomi −5.3% — and Zijin Mining off 8.2%. What rose were banks and utilities: ICBC, China Mobile, Yangtze Power and AgBank each up a fraction. That is the classic defensive shift, money leaving growth for regulated, dividend-paying, state-linked names. Shenzhen closed +0.26% while Shanghai fell 0.99%, a mild divergence between the two mainland boards worth watching if it persists."
