   "insight": {
    "headline": "The Nikkei ran away from everyone",
    "body": "Japan's +4.74% dwarfs every other index move today and is the outlier worth explaining rather than ignoring. More instructive for an Indian reader: gold rose 1.44% while both Brent and WTI fell. Those usually move together when Middle East risk drives the tape, so the split suggests gold is being bought on rate expectations rather than war fear. Europe did not move as a bloc — the DAX gained while the FTSE and CAC fell. Bitcoin slipped 1.77%."
